r service at 1-954-429-2000.  SET's number for this recall is SET17B.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":3547,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=17V425000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":12,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2012","make":"TOYOTA","model":"TACOMA"},{"year":"2011","make":"TOYOTA","model":"4RUNNER"},{"year":"2011","make":"TOYOTA","model":"TACOMA"},{"year":"2012","make":"TOYOTA","model":"4RUNNER"},{"year":"2013","make":"TOYOTA","model":"TACOMA"},{"year":"2014","make":"TOYOTA","model":"TACOMA"},{"year":"2014","make":"TOYOTA","model":"4RUNNER"},{"year":"2015","make":"TOYOTA","model":"4RUNNER"},{"year":"2015","make":"TOYOTA","model":"TACOMA"},{"year":"2013","make":"TOYOTA","model":"4RUNNER"},{"year":"2016","make":"TOYOTA","model":"TACOMA"},{"year":"2016","make":"TOYOTA","model":"4RUNNER"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"17V356000","received":"2017-06-01","manufacturer":"Toyota Motor Engineering & Manufacturing","component":"ENGINE","summary":"Toyota Motor Engineering & Manufacturing (Toyota) is recalling certain 2016-2017 Tacoma vehicles equipped with a six-cylinder engine.  The affected vehicles have a crank position sensor that may malfunction, potentially resulting in an engine stall.","consequence":"An engine stall may increase the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Toyota will notify owners, and dealers will replace the crank position sensor with an improved design, free of charge.  The recall began July 26, 2017.  Owners may contact Toyota customer service at 1-800-331-4331.  Toyota's number for this recall is H0H.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":31824,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=17V356000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":2,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"TACOMA"},{"year":"2016","make":"TOYOTA","model":"TACOMA"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"17V285000","received":"2017-04-27","manufacturer":"Toyota Motor Engineering & Manufacturing","component":"POWER TRAIN:DRIVELINE:DIFFERENTIAL UNIT","summary":"Toyota Motor Engineering & Manufacturing (Toyota) is recalling certain 2016-2017 Tacoma vehicles.  Oil may leak from the area where the rear differential carrier is assembled to rear axle housing.","consequence":"If the vehicle is operated with an insufficient amount of oil in the rear differential, the differential may seize and cause a loss of control, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Toyota will notify owners, and dealers will inspect the rear differential for oil leakage.  Based on the inspection, dealers will either tightening the fastening nuts or replace the fastening nuts and gasket.  If the rear differential components are damaged, the rear differential carrier assembly will be replaced.  The repairs will be performed free of charge.  The recall June 19, 2017.  Owners may contact Toyota customer service at 1-800-331-4331.  Toyota's number for this recall is H0G.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":227732,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=17V285000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":2,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"TACOMA"},{"year":"2016","make":"TOYOTA","model":"TACOMA"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"15V656000","received":"2015-10-14","manufacturer":"Toyota Motor Engineering & Manufacturing","component":"AIR BAGS:KNEE BOLSTER","summary":"Toyota Motor Engineering & Manufacturing (Toyota) is recalling certain model year 2016 Tacoma trucks manufactured August 20, 2015, to September 10, 2015.  In the affected vehicles, incorrect bolts were used to install the driver's knee air bag module.","consequence":"The incorrect bolts may loosen over time and affect the performance of the driver's knee air bag, increasing the risk of driver injury during a crash that necessitates deployment of the air bags.","remedy":"Toyota will notify owners, and dealers will install the correct driver's knee air bag module mounting bolts, free of charge.  The recall began on November 19, 2015.  Owners may contact Toyota customer service at 1-800-331-4331. Toyota's number for this recall is F0T.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":306,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=15V656000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":1,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2016","make":"TOYOTA","model":"TACOMA"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false}]}
